# The event log tools/windows-state.ps1 writes (D79, SPEC-QUESTIONS P2-2,
# P2-3): every level, a message over two lines, an empty message, an event
# whose source has no message file, and one whose source was removed.
get event log entries from "OtterW5" up to 20 into entries
for each entry in entries
    say source of entry "|" level of entry "|" time of entry "|" message of entry
.
get event log entries from "OtterW5" up to 3 into entries
say length of entries "of the newest"
get event log entries from "OtterW5*" up to 50 into entries
say length of entries "through a wildcard"
get event log entries from "OtterW5 Empty" up to 5 into entries
say length of entries "in the empty log"
try
    get event log entries from "OtterW5 No Such Log" up to 5 into entries
otherwise into reason
    say reason
.
